{"id": "child-care-money-with-no-names", "title": "Child care: most of the money is paid onward to recipients the public record does not name", "seconds": 130.2, "voice": "elevenlabs:9PVP7ENhDskL0KYHAKtD", "narrator": "Jerry B.", "tempo": 1.087, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "efd3d4d10bf528e9", "words": 402, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[2]"], "text": "San Francisco has fewer young children now.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 2.15, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["children under five, 2019", "36,864"], "b": ["children under five, 2026", "32,320"]}, "emph": ["fewer"], "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.73, 0.89, 1.16, 1.36, 1.69]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[2]"], "text": "36,864 under five in 2019.", "t0": 2.27, "t1": 5.66, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["children under five, 2019", "36,864"], "b": ["children under five, 2026", "32,320"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.49, 0.87, 1.04, 1.27, 1.94, 2.16, 2.46, 2.56, 2.83]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[2]"], "text": "32,320 today.", "t0": 5.78, "t1": 7.93, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["children under five, 2019", "36,864"], "b": ["children under five, 2026", "32,320"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.5, 0.97, 1.23, 1.5, 1.79]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "But City child-care payments climbed.", "t0": 8.05, "t1": 9.74, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "City child-care payments", "sub": "$117.7 million in fiscal 2019"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.39, 0.88, 1.23]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "117.7 million dollars in 2019. And in fiscal 2026?", "t0": 9.86, "t1": 15.54, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "City child-care payments", "sub": "$117.7 million in fiscal 2019"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.46, 0.98, 1.24, 1.55, 1.86, 2.19, 2.29, 2.55, 3.56, 3.8, 3.93, 4.3, 4.57]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "suspicious[1]"], "text": "297.3 million dollars.", "t0": 15.54, "t1": 18.05, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$297.3 million", "label": "City early-childhood payments, fiscal 2026", "sub": "$3,192 per child under five then; $9,198 now"}, "emph": ["297.3"], "wt": [0.04, 0.24, 0.5, 1.11, 1.36, 1.73, 2.09]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 18.57, "t1": 20.19, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.3, 0.39, 0.95, 1.14, 1.21]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "innocent[2]"], "text": "Voters chose that. Proposition C, a tax on commercial rents, pays for early care.", "t0": 20.31, "t1": 24.95, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Proposition C", "sub": "a commercial rents tax for early care"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.39, 0.66, 1.32, 1.88, 2.29, 2.42, 2.7, 2.82, 3.27, 3.73, 3.98, 4.13, 4.37]}, {"scene": "money", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]", "story[2]"], "text": "83 percent goes to three agencies. The City pays the agency.", "t0": 25.17, "t1": 28.8, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "City and State", "sub": "pay the agency"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Children's Council of San Francisco", "sub": "the largest agency"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "Centres and homes", "sub": "the one a family chose"}], "kicker": "How child-care money moves"}, "emph": ["83 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.52, 0.9, 1.12, 1.25, 1.52, 2.32, 2.48, 2.77, 3.01, 3.14]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]"], "text": "The biggest is Children’s Council of San Francisco. In 2025, how much did it pay onward?", "t0": 29.02, "t1": 34.85, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Children's Council of San Francisco", "kicker": "The first lead", "sub": "its 2025 tax return", "chip": "$209.7 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.51, 0.64, 1.04, 1.38, 1.47, 1.66, 2.76, 2.93, 3.2, 4.08, 4.27, 4.46, 4.61, 4.71, 4.95]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "186.8 million dollars.", "t0": 34.85, "t1": 37.12, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$186.8 million", "label": "paid onward, 2025", "sub": "89% of its spending"}, "emph": ["186.8"], "wt": [0.04, 0.24, 0.5, 1.05, 1.33, 1.53, 1.89]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "To whom? One line of its tax return reads:", "t0": 37.64, "t1": 40.8, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Child care Subsidies and Child care Provider Stipends: 2,547 recipients, $100.6 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 1.19, 1.43, 1.65, 1.75, 1.9, 2.15, 2.5]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "2,547 recipients, 100.6 million dollars.", "t0": 40.8, "t1": 45.11, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Child care Subsidies and Child care Provider Stipends: 2,547 recipients, $100.6 million"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.27, 0.66, 0.92, 1.17, 1.77, 2.6, 2.83, 3.07, 3.34, 3.61, 3.93]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "No names.", "t0": 45.23, "t1": 45.82, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Child care Subsidies and Child care Provider Stipends: 2,547 recipients, $100.6 million"}, "emph": ["No names"], "wt": [0.0, 0.2]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["innocent[0]"], "text": "That’s because the form asks for a count and a total, not names.", "t0": 45.94, "t1": 49.12, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "grants to individuals: a kind of grant, a number of recipients and a total"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.53, 0.66, 1.02, 1.21, 1.37, 1.44, 1.7, 1.8, 1.89, 2.5, 2.79]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why"], "text": "So no one outside can see which centres were paid, or for how many children.", "t0": 49.24, "t1": 52.9, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Who was paid, for how many children?", "kicker": "The first lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.37, 0.5, 0.95, 1.1, 1.29, 1.49, 1.78, 1.93, 2.49, 2.74, 2.9, 3.05, 3.24]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[6]"], "text": "Its audits record 77.3 million federal dollars through the City.", "t0": 53.02, "t1": 56.67, "shot": "b10b", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["federal money its audits record through the City", "$77.3 million"], "b": ["named in the City’s subaward reports", "$275,000"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.49, 0.88, 1.52, 1.77, 2.05, 2.4, 2.72, 3.03, 3.23, 3.33]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "No record counts funded children at each centre. So test the money against the licence.", "t0": 56.89, "t1": 60.93, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Faces SF", "kicker": "The second lead", "sub": "State contracts, 2025-26", "chip": "$15.6 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.48, 0.76, 1.07, 1.41, 1.52, 1.68, 2.32, 2.58, 2.82, 2.94, 3.18, 3.44, 3.55]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what"], "text": "Faces SF has State contracts worth 15.6 million dollars.", "t0": 61.05, "t1": 64.59, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Faces SF", "kicker": "The second lead", "sub": "at the City’s top rate, $36,324 a year"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.44, 0.69, 0.88, 1.0, 1.26, 1.72, 1.92, 2.34, 2.6, 2.86, 3.13]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what"], "text": "At the City’s top rate, how many children is that?", "t0": 64.71, "t1": 67.59, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Faces SF", "kicker": "The second lead", "sub": "at the City’s top rate, $36,324 a year"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.27, 0.57, 0.88, 1.35, 1.52, 1.72, 2.06, 2.18]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what"], "text": "428.", "t0": 67.59, "t1": 68.66, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "428", "label": "full-time children the money could pay for", "sub": "against 271 licensed places"}, "emph": ["428"], "wt": [0.04, 0.29, 0.55]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2].why"], "text": "Its licences hold 271.", "t0": 69.18, "t1": 71.17, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["children the contracts could pay for", "428"], "b": ["places on its licences", "271"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.69, 0.9, 1.11, 1.36]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2].why"], "text": "A place can serve two part-day children, so a gap that size needs a written reason.", "t0": 71.29, "t1": 75.23, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["children the contracts could pay for", "428"], "b": ["places on its licences", "271"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.36, 0.49, 0.75, 0.95, 1.38, 2.02, 2.25, 2.33, 2.57, 2.75, 3.07, 3.26, 3.32, 3.57]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]"], "text": "Then Companeros Del Barrio. Its licence closed in December 2024.", "t0": 75.45, "t1": 79.3, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "Companeros Del Barrio", "kicker": "The third lead", "sub": "licence closed 2024-12-10"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.75, 0.92, 1.61, 1.85, 2.21, 2.54, 2.63, 3.04, 3.31]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[7]"], "text": "A contract holder of that name is still listed for State money.", "t0": 79.42, "t1": 82.13, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "Companeros Del Barrio Inc", "kicker": "The third lead", "sub": "State allocation, 2025-26 and 2026-27", "chip": "$2,591,980"}, "emph": ["still listed"], "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.6, 0.87, 0.97, 1.16, 1.39, 1.49, 1.74, 2.02, 2.16, 2.44]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "notEstablished[5]"], "text": "The records do not show whether this is the same organisation.", "t0": 82.25, "t1": 85.13, "shot": "b15b", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "The allocation table gives a name and a county, no address or licence number.", "kicker": "Matched by name"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.51, 0.71, 0.91, 1.17, 1.47, 1.66, 1.78, 1.91, 2.18]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[0]"], "text": "In 2019 the Controller found 69 of 579 providers potentially over capacity.", "t0": 85.35, "t1": 90.62, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "69", "label": "of 579 subsidised providers potentially over licensed capacity", "sub": "City Controller, 2019"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.41, 0.89, 1.01, 1.49, 1.73, 2.34, 2.43, 2.68, 2.94, 3.45, 3.95, 4.52, 4.71]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "established[0]"], "text": "The school district’s auditor found no papers for 28 of 47 child-care charges.", "t0": 90.74, "t1": 95.07, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "School district auditor, fiscal 2022", "sub": "28 of 47 sampled charges undocumented", "chip": "$6,711,381"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.39, 0.77, 1.14, 1.4, 1.58, 1.95, 2.1, 2.62, 2.72, 3.35, 3.85]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "established[0]"], "text": "Likely questioned costs: 6,711,381 dollars.", "t0": 95.19, "t1": 98.18, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "School district auditor, fiscal 2022", "sub": "28 of 47 sampled charges undocumented", "chip": "$6,711,381"}, "emph": ["6,711,381"], "wt": [0.0, 0.33, 0.68, 1.24, 1.54, 1.78, 2.03, 2.32, 2.61]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[8]"], "text": "The district’s later audits call that partly corrected. Whether any money was repaid isn’t stated.", "t0": 98.3, "t1": 103.31, "shot": "b19b", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "School district audits, 2022-23 and 2023-24", "sub": "partly corrected; repayment not stated"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.58, 0.88, 1.2, 1.46, 1.59, 1.91, 2.85, 3.17, 3.38, 3.65, 3.83, 4.33, 4.55]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "count", "ref": ["established[4]"], "text": "State error-rate studies sampled 6 San Francisco contractor-years. 2 had errors; no review found fraud.", "t0": 103.43, "t1": 109.11, "shot": "b19e", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "2", "label": "of 6 sampled San Francisco contractor-years with errors", "sub": "State error-rate studies, 2021-22 and 2022-23"}, "emph": ["2 had errors"], "wt": [0.0, 0.33, 0.79, 1.13, 1.48, 1.69, 1.87, 2.38, 3.59, 3.82, 3.97, 4.55, 4.77, 5.06, 5.31]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[5]"], "text": "In March 2023, the department sought a 300 million dollar contractor to pay out workforce money.", "t0": 109.23, "t1": 114.53, "shot": "b19f", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "cs1", "kicker": "Civil Service Commission, 20 March 2023", "text": "Request 47273-22/23: $300.0 million of “Administrative Services- Fiscal Intermediary”", "mark": "$300.0 million"}, "emph": ["300 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.41, 0.67, 1.56, 1.69, 2.14, 2.35, 2.42, 2.66, 2.94, 3.23, 3.51, 4.08, 4.18, 4.37, 4.54, 5.03]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "Nothing shows a provider paid for children it didn’t serve. Or that the closed licence was paid.", "t0": 114.75, "t1": 119.27, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any provider was paid for children it did not serve", "That the closed licence was ever paid"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.56, 0.62, 1.06, 1.25, 1.38, 1.73, 1.84, 2.1, 2.83, 3.06, 3.21, 3.32, 3.67, 4.01, 4.15]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? Payments by provider, and funded children at each site.", "t0": 119.39, "t1": 123.25, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Payments by provider and funded children by site"}, {"who": "", "what": "Each agency’s list of providers paid over $100,000"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.32, 0.6, 1.19, 1.57, 1.74, 2.34, 2.57, 2.93, 3.3, 3.4, 3.57]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "No authority has found money missing. The count by site is the missing link.", "t0": 123.37, "t1": 127.04, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.58, 0.7, 0.93, 1.16, 1.81, 2.0, 2.26, 2.46, 2.77, 2.92, 3.06, 3.4]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 127.16, "t1": 129.34, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.35, 0.46, 0.53, 1.19, 1.41, 1.5]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "money": "Where it goes", "lead1": "Lead 1 · $186.8 million, no names", "lead2": "Lead 2 · 428 children, 271 places", "lead3": "Lead 3 · a closed licence", "found": "Official findings", "check": "A check that came back clean", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "kinetic", "hook": "contrast"}